<title>USA: Continental, Alitalia expand partnership.</title>
<headline>Continental, Alitalia expand partnership.</headline>
<dateline>NEWARK, N.J. 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Continental Airlines Inc and Alitalia - Linee Aeree Italiane SpA said Thursday they have expanded their partnership and will increase their joint capacity to three daily, non-stop flights between New York and Rome and Milan.</p>
<p>The expansion will begin in the summer of 1997, the said.</p>
<p>With the addition, Continental and Alitalia will jointly offer twice-daily flights to Rome and a daily flight to Milan.</p>
<p>All of the flights will depart from Newark International Airport using Continental DC-10-30 aircraft. The two carriers will share passenger and cargo capacity.</p>
<p>Continental and Alitalia currently codeshare one daily non-stop flight between Newark and Rome and one to Milan.</p>
</text>
